#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:1
msgid "Installing Gazebo11 side by side with new Gazebo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:3
msgid "Supported Gazebo versions and Ubuntu platforms for this tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:5
msgid ""
"This tutorial affects the Gazebo Classic users on Ubuntu `Jammy` (latest "
"Ubuntu release were Gazebo Classic packages supported by the Gazebo team) "
"that plan on migrating code to new Gazebo `Fortress`, `Garden` or `Harmonic.`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:9
msgid ""
"There is no guarantee that the Gazebo Classic version detailed in this "
"document will be updated in any case. Please consider the migration to the "
"new Gazebo as the recommended alternative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:13
msgid "General context and migrations to new Gazebo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:15
msgid ""
"New versions of Gazebo can not be installed together with Gazebo Classic  "
"(aka `gazebo11`) since both use the `gz` command line tool. Trying to  "
"install `gz-garden` or `gz-harmonic` from `packages.osrfoundation.org`  on a "
"system that already has gazebo-classic installed from binaries  will cause "
"gazebo-classic and its dependencies to be uninstalled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:21
msgid ""
"Having a side by side installation of both can make easier the recommended "
"migration to newer versions of Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:24
msgid "Alternative approach for Gazebo Classic without the gz tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:26
msgid ""
"A possible workaround could be to use Gazebo Classic without the `gz` "
"command or with a renamed `gz` command. This can be particularly interesting "
"since the ROS (Robot Operative System) wrapper known as `gazebo_ros_pkgs` do "
"not use the `gz` command but the `gzserver` and `gzclient` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:32
msgid ""
"Not shipping the `gz` command by default in a Gazebo Classic installation "
"would be a disruptive change for existing users so it should not be hosted "
"in `packages.osrfoundation.org`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:36
msgid "Gazebo11 with a separate gz tool package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:38
msgid ""
"This alterntive approach has been implemented and packages for `jammy` are "
"hosted in the Open Robotics `gazebo11-gz-cli` PPA: https://launchpad.net/"
"~openrobotics/+archive/ubuntu/gazebo11-gz-cli"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:42
msgid ""
"The PPA contains a `gazebo11` version that ships the `gz` executable in an "
"independent packages called `gazebo11-gz-cli` while the main `gazebo11` "
"package has a `gz11` command. Both are really symlinks to `gz-11.x.y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:46
msgid "How the packaging works for the gz command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:48
msgid ""
"The `gazebo11-gz-cli` is a soft dependency on `gazebo11`. It is installed by "
"default but it will be uninstalled when installing the new Gazebo  packages "
"and the effect is that the `gz` command for Gazebo Classic replaced  by the "
"`gz` tool from new Gazebo. The `gz11` command can be used instead of the "
"`gz` command to access to the same functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:54
msgid "Installing the new packaging from the PPA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:56
msgid ""
"From an existing `gazebo11` installation (on `jammy` the Ubuntu official "
"repositories will install `11.10.2+dfsg-1` version) or a non existing "
"`gazebo11` installation the steps are the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:60
msgid ""
"sudo add-apt-repository ppa:openrobotics/gazebo11-gz-cli\n"
"sudo apt update\n"
"sudo apt-get install gazebo11\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:66
msgid ""
"If `gazebo11` was installed before, it will be upgraded to the version in "
"the PPA. From this point, a new Gazebo installation for `fortress`, `garden` "
"or `harmonic` can be executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_gz11_side_by_side.md:70
msgid ""
"If a new Gazebo installation was installed before, the `gazebo11-gz-cli` "
"package won't be installed."
msgstr ""
